# Web Deployment Protocol

## When to Deploy
- After ANY change to files in mobile/lib/
- After ANY change to files in dashboard/
- After backend changes that affect client-facing APIs
- NEVER deploy without building first

## Deployment Command (canonical — committed in repo)

From project root:

```bash
bash scripts/deploy_flutter_web.sh
```

This runs: `flutter build web --release` → stamps `version.json` → `rsync` to **`/var/www/sovereignsanctuary-web/`** on GREEN (coach + app portals per host nginx) → `nginx reload` → **`scripts/cf_purge_flutter_web.sh`** when purge credentials exist.

Flags: `--no-build` (rsync existing `mobile/build/web` only), `--no-purge` (skip Cloudflare API purge).

**Legacy:** A personal **`./deploy-web.sh`** may still exist locally (often **gitignored**); it is **not** the source of truth and older copies wrongly targeted **`/var/www/coach-portal/`** for Flutter — **do not use that path** for `coach.*` / `app.*` (see `flutter-build-verification.mdc`).

**`/ws`** is the **bridge WebSocket URL** (and Cloudflare LB pin to primary). It is **not** a shell deploy command.

## Pre-Deploy Checklist
1. All changes committed to git
2. Protected files verified (bridge_server.py, main.py, littlenate_inference.py max line budgets checked)
3. `flutter build web` compiles without errors
4. No uncommitted changes to .cursorrules protected files

## Backend Deployment (separate from web)
Backend files deploy via scp to GREEN individually:
```bash
scp <file> root@68.183.168.75:/opt/clinical-sovereignty-lab/<path>
ssh root@68.183.168.75 "docker compose -f /opt/clinical-sovereignty-lab/docker-compose.prod.yml restart backend && sleep 8 && docker logs nate_backend --tail 5"
```

Dashboard HTML files deploy to BOTH locations:
```bash
scp <file> root@68.183.168.75:/opt/clinical-sovereignty-lab/dashboard/
scp <file> root@68.183.168.75:/var/www/sovereign-command/
```

## Post-Deploy Verification
1. Check backend health: 104/104 services
2. Verify app loads: https://app.sovereignsanctuary.net
3. Verify command loads: https://command.sovereignsanctuary.net
4. Test the specific feature that was changed
5. Check browser console for errors (F12)

## NEVER
- Deploy without committing first
- Skip the cache purge (users will see stale content at the edge — use `scripts/cf_purge_flutter_web.sh` or dashboard purge)
- Deploy dashboard files to only one location (must go to BOTH `/opt/.../dashboard/` and `/var/www/sovereign-command/` per `deployment-safety.mdc`)
- Put Cloudflare **purge** secrets in a committed file — use **`CLOUDFLARE_PURGE_TOKEN`** in repo-root `.env` only
